### JetBrains HTTP client / VS Code REST Client – start the API first: uv run fastapi dev

### Health
GET http://localhost:8000/health/ready

### REST: create a user
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "alice", "email": "alice@example.com"}

### REST: create an item (price as string – exact decimal)
POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/items
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Keyboard", "price": "49.90", "owner_id": 1}

### REST: one user with items
GET http://localhost:8000/api/v1/users/1

### REST: search + pagination
GET http://localhost:8000/api/v1/users?q=ali&limit=10&offset=0

### REST: partial update
PATCH http://localhost:8000/api/v1/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"role": "admin"}

### GraphQL: nested query – the client picks the fields
POST http://localhost:8000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query": "{ users { username items { title price } } }"}

### GraphQL: mutation
POST http://localhost:8000/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query": "mutation { createItem(input: {title: \"Mouse\", price: \"19.99\", ownerId: 1}) { id title price } }"}

### Protobuf: binary response (use demo_client.py to decode)
GET http://localhost:8000/api/v1/proto/users/1
